  "description": "The owner approves the change story chg-1 on Friday, which ends its period, and the architect approves it again on Saturday, which records nothing. The owner's approval is withdrawn on Monday while the architect's remains in effect: no period begins, the withdrawal records no begin act and is cited by none, and the story still reads ended by the owner's review, reviewed and not pending. When the architect's approval is withdrawn on Wednesday, no review remains in effect: the second period begins then, cause review_withdrawn, citing that withdrawal, and the story is open, unreviewed and pending. Earlier cutoffs read as before.",
  "note": "Step 7: 7.6.2: \"Once a period has ended, the next begins at the effective time of the first withdrawal of a review that leaves no review of the story in effect (6.7.9, 7.2.7). No period begins while another review remains in effect.\" Step 13: 7.6.4: `review_withdrawn` \"The record is the withdrawal whose taking effect left no review of the story in effect\". The first period keeps its end act citing the owner's review (7.6.2: a period ends at the first review in effect, which that review was).",
